===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|it|omertà}} – even though a further etymology is disputed – italianization of {{bor|en|scn|umirtà}} (“the quality of being humble, quiet, soft”). Some see it as a southern dialectal variant of {{m|it|umiltà||humility}}, from {{der|en|la|humilitās}}, from {{m|la|humilis||humble}}, from {{m|la|humus||ground, soil}}, in which case it is a {{doublet|en|humility|nocap=1}}. Other sources (as the [[OED]]) interpret it as a Sicilian [[calque]] ([[loan translation]]) of {{noncog|es|hombredad||[[manliness]]}}, altered to fit {{noncog|scn|omu||man}}; in this latter case though “''ummirità''” should be the natural phonological output.

