|en
|date=March 4, 2005
|work=Boston Globe
|passage=Patriarca pleaded guilty in December 1991 to racketeering and conspiracy charges, but he refused to admit he was a member of the Mafia, clinging to his vow of ‘'''omerta'''’ to the secret organization.
}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=October 27, 2006
|work=Los Angeles Times
|passage=There was a time that high-profile killings such as the 1968 assassinations of Robert F. Kennedy and Martin Luther King Jr. brought passionate cries for limitations on handguns. A bipartisan '''omerta''' now smothers the issue.
}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=October 2016
|url=http://www.scientificamerican.com/article/how-the-fda-manipulates-the-media/
|title=How the FDA Manipulates the Media
|work=Scientific American
|passage=The FDA was not pleased that the '''omertà''' had been broken.
}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Heather Stewart|quotee=w:Sadiq Khan|title=‘Choose London’: Sadiq Khan steps up efforts to lure EU citizens post-Brexit|work=The Guardian|date=2023-10-06|url=https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2023/oct/06/london-sadiq-khan-eu-citizens-uk-capital-brexit-mayor|issn=0261-3077|passage=Despite criticising what he called an “'''omertà'''” in British politics about Brexit, he expressed some sympathy for the Labour leader Keir’s wariness about the issue.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Kim Willsher|quotee=w:Judith Godrèche|title=Judith Godrèche to address French cinema’s ‘omertà’ around #MeToo|work=The Guardian|date=2024-02-21|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/feb/21/judith-godreche-to-address-france-silence-around-metoo-cesar-awards|issn=0261-3077|passage=Judith Godrèche, an actor who has accused two high-profile directors of raping her as a teenager, will address France’s most prestigious film awards ceremony on Friday in an unusual move aimed at breaking what she calls the “'''omertà'''” surrounding the abuse of women and girls in the industry.}}

