==Sicilian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|scn|umirtà}}

===Etymology===
Ultimately, a {{doublet|nocap=1|scn|umiltati|t1=humility, humbleness}}. Possibly borrowed, or at least influenced, from {{bor|scn|it|omertà}}, itself from {{der|scn|nap|-}}. Possibly later reanalyzed by [[mafioso|mafiosi]] as deriving from {{m|scn|omu|t=man}}, thus implying that people who are not [[reticent]] are not men, thus [[coward]]s.

===Noun===
{{scn-noun|omertà|f|}} {{tlb|scn|uncountable}}

# {{lb|scn|mafia}} [[#English|omertà]] (condition by which one should follow a [[code of silence]])

